[X] Preserve injectable jitter behavior\n  Verification:\n    - [X] Re-run pytest suite\n    - [X] Write root cause report"}],"details":{"op":"done","phases":[{"name":"Investigation","tasks":[{"content":"Run pytest suite","status":"completed"},{"content":"Inspect flaky queue implementation","status":"completed"},{"content":"Identify nondeterministic ordering source","status":"completed"}]},{"name":"Fix","tasks":[{"content":"Make task ordering deterministic","status":"completed"},{"content":"Make retry scheduling deterministic","status":"completed"},{"content":"Preserve injectable jitter behavior","status":"completed"}]},{"name":"Verification","tasks":[{"content":"Re-run pytest suite","status":"completed"},{"content":"Write root cause report","status":"completed"}]}],"storage":"memory","completedTasks":[{"phase":"Verification","content":"Re-run pytest suite"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788199347884},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CNfeEleDnwDpJwVH9BHncZnf|fc_02882f0bf381b985016a95c1b3b55487d2905669110c0da806","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[root_cause.md#53CB]\n1:# Flaky pytest root cause\n2:\n3:## Flaky behavior\n4:`Scheduler.ready()` could return equal-priority tasks in different orders across calls, and `Scheduler.schedule_retry()` ignored injected clock/random sources. The tests expose those symptoms by expecting stable ordering and deterministic retry timestamps when fakes are injected.\n5:\n6:## Root cause\n7:Implementation in `flakyqueue/scheduler.py` mixed injected dependencies with global nondeterministic sources:\n8:\n9:- `add()` used `time.time()` instead of the injected clock.\n10:- `ready()` used `time.time()` and `random.shuffle(items)` before sorting only by priority. For equal-priority tasks, Python's stable sort preserved the shuffled order, so output order changed nondeterministically.\n11:- `schedule_retry()` used `random.random()` and `time.time()` instead of the injected random source and clock.\n12:\n13:That made