{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Fixed in `in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py`.\n\nProblem:\n- `add()` and `schedule_retry()` ignored the injected clock.\n- `schedule_retry()` ignored the injected random source.\n- `ready()` used `random.shuffle()` and then sorted only by priority, so equal-priority tasks inherited a random tie order.\n\nDecision:\n- Added `_now()` and `_jitter()` helpers.\n- Routed all time reads through `self.clock.now()`.\n- Routed retry jitter through injected `random_source`, defaulting to stdlib `random` only when none is injected.\n- Removed `random.shuffle()` from `ready()`.\n- Made ready ordering deterministic with `(-priority, run_at, created_at, id)`.\n\nWhy this fixes the flake:\n- Injected fakes now fully control creation time, readiness time, and retry jitter.\n- Equal-priority tasks no longer depend on RNG or incidental container order.\n\nVerification:\n- Ran from `/workspace/in/flakyqueue`:\n  - `PATH=/tmp/mini-bin:$PATH PYTHONPATH=/tmp/mini_pytest_pkg python -m pytest tests`\n  - Result: `4 passed`\n- Direct deterministic exercise with injected fakes produced:\n  - ready order twice: `['task-c', 'task-a', 'task-b']`\n  - retry `run_at`: `1010.25`\n  - before due time: `['task-c', 'task-b']`\n  - at due time: `['task-c', 'task-b', 'task-a']`\n\nReport:\n- Wrote `root_cause.md` to `/workspace/out/root_cause.md`.\n\nNote:\n- The harness did not provide a `python` launcher or installed `pytest`, so verification used `/usr/bin/python3` via a temporary `python` shim plus a temporary local `pytest` module, without modifying repo files or tests."}}
